---
import LessonShell from '../../layouts/LessonShell.astro';
---
<LessonShell
    course="LolRust"
    number={2}
    name="Making Variables"
    objective="Create three variables and use them in a meow! ~ name, age, and a wiggly zoomies counter."
    keywords={[
        { code: 'make', note: 'create a variable (let)' },
        { code: 'make wiggly', note: 'create a changeable variable (let mut)' },
        { code: 'meow!("...{}...", x)', note: 'print with placeholders' },
    ]}
    initial={`iz main() {
    // TODO 1: make a variable named \`name\` set to "Ada"
    // TODO 2: make a variable named \`age\` set to 25
    // TODO 3: make a WIGGLY variable named \`zoomies\` set to 9000

    meow!("hai fren! i am {} and i have {} zoomies!", name, zoomies);
}`}
    checks={[
        { label: 'has let binding', pattern: '\\blet\\s+\\w+\\s*=' },
        { label: 'has let mut for wiggly', pattern: '\\blet\\s+mut\\s+\\w+' },
        { label: 'transpiled meow!', pattern: '\\bprintln!' },
        { label: 'no leftover make keywords', pattern: '\\bmake\\b', negate: true },
    ]}
    prev={{ href: '/lolrust/lesson-1', label: 'lesson 1' }}
    next={{ href: '/lolrust/lesson-3', label: 'lesson 3' }}
    hints={[
        'Use `make name = ...;` to declare a normal variable.',
        '`zoomies` needs to be wiggly because it can change. Use `make wiggly`.',
        'Strings need quotes: `make name = "Ada";`. Numbers don\'t: `make age = 25;`.',
    ]}
    solution={`iz main() {
    make name = "Ada";
    make age = 25;
    make wiggly zoomies = 9000;

    meow!("hai fren! i am {} and i have {} zoomies!", name, zoomies);
}`}
/>
